Andrew Schofield resolved KAFKA-18761.
--------------------------------------
    Resolution: Fixed

> kafka-share-groups.sh --describe only shows offset information when members exist
> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-18761
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-18761
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Sub-task
>    Affects Versions: 4.1.0
>            Reporter: Andrew Schofield
>            Assignee: Andrew Schofield
>            Priority: Major
>             Fix For: 4.1.0
>
>
> When kafka-share-groups.sh is used to describe the offsets for the share-partitions in the group, it uses the list of assigned partitions for the active members to build the list of offsets. The problem with this is that when there are no active members, the list of partitions is empty and no offset information is shown.
> The tool should change to list all offsets for the share group, irrespective of the current state of the members. This actually will require changes in the broker so that it can return the offset information for all share-partitions.



--
