Subject: Re: kafka 4.0.0 running on java 11
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

No. Kafka 4.0 only supports Java 17 and above.

Note that if you're still using JDK11, you probably are no longer receiv=
ing security updates. All of the major vendors have declared it EOL. So =
you are probably out of compliance with security guidelines.

[Some vendors offer extended support for a price, so if you're in that s=
ituation, please ignore the above.]

best,
Colin


