Hi Colin,

Thanks for the KIP. It=E2=80=99s good to give users more flexibility to =
downgrade metadata.version.

PY1: Each feature has bootstrapMetadataVersion. For example, TV_2 is =
IBP_4_0_IV2.
Assume that a cluster uses TV_2 and metadata.version 4.0-IV2. If a user =
downgrades
metadata.version to 3.9-IV0, will the controller check =
TransactionVersion and reject
the request?

PY2: After users downgrade metadata.version, can they also restart =
server with old binary
version? If they can, we need to add related end-to-end ducktape test.

Thanks,
PoAn

