--------------------------------------

             Summary: Implementation of a Simple, Low-Latency Bounded Share=
d Buffer
                 Key: KAFKA-19134
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19134
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: New Feature
            Reporter: Chia-Ping Tsai
            Assignee: Chia-Ping Tsai


Using the shared buffer in the network threads can reduce the GC count (and=
 elapsed time). The attached patch offers a simple memory pool based on Con=
currentSkipListMap, and in my small env (1000000000 records), the GC time i=
s reduced from 127.808 ms to 93.608 ms), and the created bytes are reduced =
from 40GB to 2GB.

