Subject: EmbeddedConnectCluster with multiple Connectors
To: dev@kafka.apache.org
Content-Type: multipart/alternative; boundary="0000000000003d515f0632bb9766"

--0000000000003d515f0632bb9766
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"

Greetings,

I am looking to run the EmbeddedClusterConnect with 2 different Connectors
in an effort to prove round trip processing across a sink and a source
connector.  However, I don't see any way to create 2 different connectors
within the cluster.

Am I missing something or has this just not been considered in the past.  I
can't find any mention of such on the mailing list.

If there is a good reason not to run 2 different connectors I would like to
hear the reasoning.  Otherwise I will propose a change to
EmbeddedConnectCluster to handle such a case.

Thank you for your time,
Claude

--0000000000003d515f0632bb9766--

