Fredrik Lys=C3=A9n created KAFKA-19188:
-------------------------------------

             Summary: kafka-topics.sh --describe output for message.format.=
version is inconsistent immediately after cluster restart when not set at t=
opic level
                 Key: KAFKA-19188
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19188
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: admin
    Affects Versions: 3.9.0
         Environment: Amazon Linux 2 (EC2 instances)
            Reporter: Fredrik Lys=C3=A9n


When running=C2=A0{{kafka-topics.sh --describe}} to inspect topic configura=
tion immediately after restarting a Kafka broker, the {{}}
{code:java}
message.format.version{code}
{{}}=C2=A0property is inconsistently present in the output.



*Steps to reproduce:*
 # Set up a 3-broker Kafka cluster.
 # On brokers 1 and 2, set=C2=A0{{log.message.format.version=3D3.2}}=C2=A0i=
n=C2=A0{{{}server.properties{}}}.
 # On broker 3 (the one you will use as=C2=A0{{{}--bootstrap-server{}}}), d=
o=C2=A0*not*=C2=A0set=C2=A0{{{}log.message.format.version{}}}.
 # Create a topic without setting=C2=A0{{message.format.version}}=C2=A0at t=
he topic level.
 # Restart the cluster.
 # Immediately after restart, run:

{code:java}
kafka-topics.sh --bootstrap-server <broker-3>:9092 --describe --command-con=
fig <config> {code}
 * Observe the output for the topic configuration.

*Expected behavior:*
The=C2=A0{{message.format.version}}=C2=A0property should be reported consis=
tently (either always present or always absent) in the topic config output,=
 reflecting the inherited value from the broker configuration when not set =
at the topic level.

*Actual behavior:*
Immediately after restart, the output for the topic sometimes omits=C2=A0{{=
message.format.version}}=C2=A0in the config list, or shows it inconsistentl=
y between runs, even though the brokers' configs are stable and the cluster=
 is healthy after a short delay.

*Additional notes:*
 * After waiting for the cluster to stabilize, the config output becomes co=
nsistent.
 * This inconsistency may cause confusion for operational monitoring or aut=
omation tools that depend on the output of=C2=A0{{{}kafka-topics.sh --descr=
ibe{}}}.

*Example output:*
{code:java}
# Immediately after restart:
Topic: example.topic =C2=A0Configs: min.insync.replicas=3D2,segment.bytes=
=3D536870912,unclean.leader.election.enable=3Dfalse

# After cluster stabilizes:
Topic: example.topic =C2=A0Configs: min.insync.replicas=3D2,segment.bytes=
=3D536870912,message.format.version=3D3.2,unclean.leader.election.enable=3D=
false {code}



