I have a question about data consistency. Kafka ISR only determines the tim=
e of lag, not the number of messages. Does ack=3Dall require the replicas i=
n the ISR to completely catch up with the number of messages or to meet the=
 time requirement? For example, if there are 3 replicas in the ISR, min.ins=
ync.replicas=3D3 and acks=3Dall, can the data of the 3 replicas be guarante=
ed to be completely consistent when the message is written? Instead of meet=
ing the replica.lag.time.max.ms time requirement.

--_000_C84F1375CE4F453A9B024EC8F25496B2itigercom_--

