hi Colin

The compatibility issue could arise if the version of the custom SLF4j
provider used by users does not match the SLF4j API version bundled with
Kafka. For example, if we upgrade the SLF4j API version to 2.x, users who
are still using slf4j-simple 1.x might encounter some issues. See the SLF4j
documentation for more details (https://www.slf4j.org/faq.html#compatibilit=
y
).

If it is not compatible, what specific actions are needed from users?


If we upgrade SLF4j to version 2.x in Kafka 5.0, users will need to ensure
that their custom SLF4j provider has released a compatible version and then
update accordingly.

Best,
Chia-Ping

