Hi Olasoji,

Thanks for updating the KIP.

2. I'm still not satisfied with the description of the public API in the
KIP. It mentions these classes:
* org.apache.kafka.common.utils.ByteBufferOutputStream
* org.apache.kafka.common.utils.ByteBufferInputStream
* org.apache.kafka.common.utils.BufferSupplier
* org.apache.kafka.common.record.CompressionType
But not any description of these classes. Please include signatures of all
new methods/variables/etc that are being exposed.

7. Does CompressionService#isAvailable returning false cause a
ConfigException? Could the CompressionService provide a reason (via an
exception) of why it isn't available, instead of returning a boolean and
requiring users to look through logs to debug the unavailability?
8. Thanks for clarifying the security model. This is just like any other
Java application, where you need to trust the JARs that you add to your
application. I don't think that the isolated classloader needs to be
mentioned in the KIP, so thank you for removing that.
9. This point does not appear to have been addressed.
10. The classes mentioned above are in existing packages that are not
exposed via Javadoc, and we have generally included whole packages in the
API at once. I think these classes need to be moved to a different package,
or removed from the API surface area.
11. The KIP states that it "also introduces an accelerated GzipCompressor".
Does this require Apache Kafka to depend on a specific accelerator
implementation? The Apache Kafka project has traditionally been very averse
to adding dependencies like this.
12. What sort of concurrency guarantees are expected from
CompressionService implementations? Should each connection, thread, or JVM
get its own instance of each CompressionService?
13. Will the existing implementations be converted to CompressionService
classes, or will they be special fallbacks? Will the default for the
configuration be "null" or some real class?
14. It looks like the new configurations are being added to the
CommonClientConfigs to be included in both producer and consumer. Where is
this configuration on the broker side? Is it a dynamic config (able to be
reconfigured via KRaft) or a static config (only configurable by
server.properties)?

Thanks,
Greg

