Just wanted to provide a short status since it's been a bit:

Luke got the last bits merged, so 3.9 is tested against Java 23.

There's a PR to move trunk to testing against Java 24 at
https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/19514. It was blocked for a while
waiting for Gradle to release, and now it's blocked waiting for the next
Spotbugs release, see
https://github.com/spotbugs/spotbugs/discussions/3380#discussioncomment-129=
98251,
I'll update the PR once 4.9.4 is out.

Running off a local build of Spotbugs, the tests pass with only a few
flakes that pass when rerun. I've backported the changes in that branch to
3.9 as well, and while we can't upgrade the CI tests until Spotbugs
releases another build, the tests do appear to pass on Java 24 for 3.9.

The only necessary change to the production code is upgrading Scala in
order to get ASM updated to a version that understands Java 24 bytecode, so
the client at least should already run fine on Java 24 on 3.9.1.

